[00:46:16] 💭  Key findings:

1. `Makefile.variables` computes `ROOTDIR` from `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`. Because `/workspace/.git` is a character device (hideGit mode), `git rev-parse` fails, so `ROOTDIR` is empty, and `Makefile.env`'s `include $(ROOTDIR)/common.env` becomes `include /common.env` which doesn't exist → `make test`/`make precommit` fail at the include stage.

2. The hideGit reminder said GOFLAGS=-buildvcs=false is "typically already set" — but here it's unset, and git commands fail. Howev…
[00:46:17] Two issues surfaced: `ROOTDIR` in `Makefile.variables` derives from `git rev-parse` (fails because `.git` is masked), leaving `ROOTDIR` empty so `include /common.env` fails; and `GOFLAGS=-buildvcs=false` is NOT set in this container despite the hideGit reminder. Let me check how dark-factory normally invokes the gate here:


[00:46:17] $ cat /workspace/.dark-factory.yaml 2>/dev/null; echo "--- log tail ---"; tail -30 /workspace/.dark-factory.log 2>/dev/null; echo "--- any env hints ---"; env | grep -iE 'rootdir|makeflags|goflags' || …
