[00:47:32] 💭 `make test` passes with `ROOTDIR=/workspace` exported. All packages compile and tests pass (`ok` for all). Interesting — GOFLAGS wasn't needed for `go test`; the go tool handled the masked .git fine (probably because it fell back gracefully, or the `-buildvcs` isn't triggering since there's no valid repo). Actually, `go build`/`go test` with a char-device `.git` — go checks for a `.git` directory, fails to read it as a dir, and treats the repo as "no VCS" → stamps `-buildvcs=false` behavior impl…
[00:47:32] `make test` passes with `ROOTDIR=/workspace` (the masked `.git` makes `git rev-parse` fail, so the env-provided `ROOTDIR` is required — exactly how the preceding prompt's container must have invoked it). My change is test-only bash, so the Go suite is unaffected.

